{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":37174434,"ns":0,"title":"Cynthia Brewer","revisions":[{"revid":1377523963,"parentid":1372237152,"minor":false,"timestamp":"2026-09-29T21:13:22Z","size":12747,"sha1":"bcc6f06a93e19125c57a1f78ab5f1099c6972e5c","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{Short description|American geographer (born 1960)}}\n{{Infobox scientist\n| honorific_prefix  = \n| name              = Cynthia Brewer\n| honorific_suffix  = \n| native_name       = \n| native_name_lang  = \n| image             = File:Cynthia Brewer - Mannerfelt Gold Medal.jpg\n| image_size        = \n| image_upright     = \n| landscape         = <!-- yes, if wide image, otherwise leave blank -->\n| alt               = \n| caption           = Cynthia Brewer receiving the ICA Carl Mannerfelt Gold Medal from outgoing ICA President Tim Trainor at the International Cartographic Conference.\n| birth_name        = <!-- if different from \"name\" -->\n| birth_date        = {{Birth year and age|1960}}\n| birth_place       = \n| death_date        = <!--{{death date and age |YYYY|MM|DD |YYYY|MM|DD}} (death date then birth date)-->\n| death_place       = \n| death_cause       = <!-- should only be included when the cause of death has significance for the subject's notability -->\n| resting_place     = \n| resting_place_coordinates = <!--{{coord|LAT|LONG|type:landmark|display=inline,title}}-->\n| other_names       = \n| siglum            = \n| pronounce         = \n| citizenship       = <!-- use only when necessary per [[WP:INFONAT]] -->\n| nationality       = <!-- use only when necessary per [[WP:INFONAT]] -->\n| fields            = \n| workplaces        = [[Pennsylvania State University]]\n| patrons           = \n| education         = [[University of Guelph]] ([[Bachelor of Arts|BA]])<br>[[Michigan State University]] ([[Master of Arts|MA]], [[PhD]])\n| thesis_title      = Prediction of Surround-Induced Changes in Map Color Appearance\n| thesis_url        = <!--(or  | thesis1_url  =   and  | thesis2_url  =  )-->\n| thesis_year       = <!--(or  | thesis1_year =   and  | thesis2_year =  )-->\n| doctoral_advisor  = <!--(or  | doctoral_advisors = )-->\n| academic_advisors = \n| doctoral_students = \n| notable_students  = \n| known_for         = [[ColorBrewer]]\n| awards            = Carl Mannerfelt Gold Medal (2023)\n| author_abbrev_bot = \n| author_abbrev_zoo = \n| spouse            = <!--(or | spouses = )-->\n| partner           = <!--(or | partners = )-->\n| children          = \n| parents           = \n| father            = \n| mother            = \n| relatives         = \n| signature         = <!--(filename only)-->\n| signature_type    = <!--(defaults to \"Signature\")-->\n| signature_alt     = \n| website           = {{URL|https://sites.psu.edu/cbrewer/}}\n| footnotes         = \n}}\n'''Cynthia Ann Brewer''' (born 1960) is an American cartographer, author, and [[professor]] of [[geography]] at [[Pennsylvania State University]]. Brewer's specialty relates to visibility and [[color theory]] in [[cartography]]. In 2023, she was awarded the [[International Cartographic Association]]'s highest honor, the [[International_Cartographic_Association#Carl_Mannerfelt_Gold_Medal|Carl Mannerfelt Gold Medal]], for her distinguished contribution to the field. \n\nHer web, print, and [[colorblind]]-friendly sets of colors, known as the Brewer palettes, have been used by numerous projects.<ref name=\"Gardner\">Stephen D. Gardner, 2005, [http://www.personal.psu.edu/cab38/ColorBrewer/Steve_Gardner_thesis_PSU.pdf Evaluation of the ColorBrewer Color Schemes for Accommodation of Map Readers with Impaired Color Vision] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180729071809/http://www.personal.psu.edu/cab38/ColorBrewer/Steve_Gardner_thesis_PSU.pdf |date=2018-07-29 }} (6.1MB PDF)</ref><ref name=\"Emily2022\">{{cite web |last1=Zaccardi |first1=Emily |title=Down from the Shelf: Accommodating Color Palettes for All |url=https://www.aag.org/down-from-the-shelf-accommodating-color-palettes-for-all/ |website=Stories |date=3 January 2022 |publisher=American Association of Geographers |access-date=2 February 2024}}</ref> She is the creator of the online color palette tool [[ColorBrewer]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=ColorBrewer 2.0 |url=https://colorbrewer2.org/# |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220630195444/https://colorbrewer2.org/#type=sequential&scheme=BuGn&n=3 |archive-date=June 30, 2022 |access-date=July 6, 2022}}</ref>\n\nBrewer has worked as a map and atlas design consultant for the [[U.S. Census Bureau]], [[National Cancer Institute]], [[National Center for Health Statistics]], and [[National Park Service]]. She teaches courses in introductory cartography and map design.<ref>{{cite book|last1=Brewer|first1=Cynthia|title=Designing Better Maps: A Guide for GIS Users|publisher=Esri Press|language=en|date=30 July 2005|id= {{ASIN|1589480899|country=uk}}}}</ref> She also works on [[topographic map]] design, multi-scale mapping, generalization, and atlas mapping. She has been influential as a theorist for map representations and [[Geographic Information System|GIS]] professionals.\n\n==Education==\nShe graduated from [[McMaster University]] (Ontario, Canada) in 1979 and the [[University of Guelph]] (Ontario, Canada) in 1983.<ref name=\"Roth2010\">{{cite journal |last1=Roth |first1=Robert E. |title=Interview with a Celebrity Cartographer: Cindy Brewer |journal=Cartographic Perspectives |date=2010 |volume=66 |issue=66 |pages=91–101 |doi=10.14714/CP66.104 |url=https://cartographicperspectives.org/index.php/journal/article/view/cp66-roth/pdf |access-date=2 February 2024|doi-access=free }}</ref> She did her master's degree in geography with emphasis in cartography at [[Michigan State University]], 1983 to 1986, presenting a thesis titled ''The Development of Process-Printed [[Munsell chart|Munsell Chart]]s for Selecting Map Colors''. After a year at [[University of California, Santa Barbara|University of California at Santa Barbara]], she obtained her doctorate from Michigan State University in 1991. Her dissertation was ''Prediction of Surround-Induced Changes in Map Color Appearance''.<ref name=\"Penn State\">{{cite web|title=Brewer, Cynthia {{!}} Penn State Department of Geography|url=http://www.geog.psu.edu/people/brewer-cynthia|website=www.geog.psu.edu|publisher=Penn State|access-date=26 February 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170320092251/http://www.geog.psu.edu/people/brewer-cynthia|archive-date=20 March 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref>\n\n==Academic career==\nShe was visiting lecturer at the [[University of California at Santa Barbara]], Department of Geography during the year 1986/87.\nOn completing her doctorate she was assistant professor, for three years (1991 to 1994) at [[San Diego State University]]. She joined the [[Pennsylvania State University]], Department of Geography in 1994 and has been professor since 2007 and was head of the department from 2014 to 2021.\n\nShe has been a faculty member of the Center of Excellence for Geospatial Information Science (CEGIS), U.S. Geological Survey, Department of Interior, since 2008.<ref name=\"Penn State\"/>\n\n==ColorBrewer==\n[[File:ColorBrewer-screenshot.png|thumb|[[ColorBrewer]] screenshot]]\n{{Main|ColorBrewer}}\n\n[[ColorBrewer]] is an online tool developed in 2002 for selecting [[thematic map]] color schemes based on Brewer's palettes.<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Miller |first1=Greg |title=The Cartographer Who's Transforming Map Design |url=https://www.wired.com/2014/10/cindy-brewer-map-design/ |magazine=Wired |access-date=31 January 2024}}</ref> The ColorBrewer palettes have uses beyond cartography; in 2018 climatologist [[Ed Hawkins (climatologist)|Ed Hawkins]] chose ColorBrewer reds and blues for [[warming stripes]] graphics portraying [[climate change|global warming]].<ref name=Voila_20191203>{{cite web |author-last=Bugden |author-first=Erica |title=Do you really understand the influential warming stripes? |url=https://www.chezvoila.com/blog/warmingstripes |website=Voilà Information Design |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191205172628/https://www.chezvoila.com/blog/warmingstripes |archive-date=5 December 2019 |date=3 December 2019 |url-status=live}}</ref>\n\n== Publications ==\n===Books===\n* {{citation|title=Designing Better Maps: A Guide for GIS Users|year=2005|last=Brewer|first=Cynthia A.|publisher=[[Esri Press]]|isbn=978-1589480896|pages=220}}\n* {{citation|title=Designed Maps: A Sourcebook for GIS Users|year=2008|last=Brewer|first=Cynthia A.|publisher=Esri Press|isbn= 978-1589481602|pages=184}}\n* {{citation|title=Designing Better Maps: A Guide for GIS Users, 2nd Edition|year=2015|last=Brewer|first=Cynthia A.|publisher=Esri Press|isbn= 978-1589484405|pages=250}}\n\n===Articles===\n* {{citation|title=ColorBrewer.org: An Online Tool for Selecting Colour Schemes for Maps|last1=Harrower|first1=Mark|last2=Brewer|first2=Cynthia A.|journal=The Cartographic Journal|volume=40|issue=1|pages=27–37|year=2003|url=http://www.albany.edu/faculty/fboscoe/papers/harrower2003.pdf|doi=10.1179/000870403235002042|bibcode=2003CartJ..40...27H |s2cid=140173239|access-date=2013-01-03|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130510171310/http://www.albany.edu/faculty/fboscoe/papers/harrower2003.pdf|archive-date=2013-05-10|url-status=dead}}\n* {{citation|title=Basic Mapping Principles for Visualizing Cancer Data Using Geographic Information Systems (GIS)|last1=Brewer|first1=Cynthia A.|journal=American Journal of Preventive Medicine|volume=30|issue=2|pages=S25–S36|year=2006|url=http://www.nrac.wvu.edu/classes/RESM440/MaterialsByWeek/Week4/Brewer_2006_BasicMappingPrinciples.pdf|doi=10.1016/j.amepre.2005.09.007|pmid=16458787|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100625180712/http://www.nrac.wvu.edu/classes/RESM440/MaterialsByWeek/Week4/Brewer_2006_BasicMappingPrinciples.pdf|archive-date=2010-06-25}}\n* {{citation|title=ColorBrewer in Print: A Catalog of Color Schemes for Maps|last1=Brewer|first1=Cynthia A.|last2=Hatchard|first2=Geoffrey W.|last3=Harrower|first3=Mark A.|journal=Cartography and Geographic Information Science|volume=30|number= 1|year=2003|pages = 5–32 (28)| doi=10.1559/152304003100010929|bibcode=2003CGISc..30....5B |s2cid=129427665}}\n* {{citation|title=A Transition in Improving Maps: The ColorBrewer Example|last1=Brewer|first1=Cynthia A.|journal=Cartography and Geographic Information Science|volume=30|number=2|year=2003|pages=159–162(4)|doi=10.1559/152304003100011126|bibcode=2003CGISc..30..159B |s2cid=62243305}}\n* {{citation|title=Guidelines for Selecting Colors for Diverging Schemes on Maps|last1=Brewer|first1=Cynthia A.|journal=The Cartographic Journal|volume=33|number=2|pages=79–86(8)|year=1996|doi=10.1179/caj.1996.33.2.79|bibcode=1996CartJ..33...79B }}\n*Olson, Judy M.; Brewer, Cynthia A. (1997). \"[http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/0004-5608.00043/abstract An Evaluation of Color Selections to Accommodate Map Users with Color-Vision Impairments]\". ''Annals of the Association of American Geographers''. 87 (1): 103–134. {{Doi|10.1111/0004-5608.00043}}.\n\n==Awards and honors==\n[[Image:Millermedal.jpg|thumb|alt=Osborn Maitland Miller Medal]]\n\n* Carl Mannerfelt Gold Medal, International Cartographic Society, 2023<ref name=\"ICA2023\">{{cite web |title=Cynthia Brewer is awarded the Carl Mannerfelt Gold Medal |url=https://icaci.org/awards/cynthia-brewer-is-awarded-the-carl-mannerfelt-gold-medal/ |website=International Cartographic Association |access-date=2 February 2024}}</ref>\n* [[Osborn Maitland Miller Medal]], American Geographical Society, 2019<ref name=\"MILLER2019\">{{cite web |title=RECIPIENTS |url=https://americangeo.org/honors/medals-and-awards/o-m-miller-medal/ |website=O.M. MILLER CARTOGRAPHIC MEDAL |publisher=American Geographical Society |access-date=2 February 2024}}</ref>\n\n== See also ==\n<!-- Please respect alphabetical o